---
layout: layouts/product.njk
title: "Conversations"
description: "Multi-channel chat sessions — SMS, MMS, WhatsApp, and in-app chat — under one Twilio-compatible REST API, with participants, messages, webhooks, and per-tenant Services."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	"serviceType": "Multi-channel chat sessions API",
	"name": "VoiceTel Conversations",
	"provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "{{ site.brand }}", "url": "{{ site.url }}" },
	"areaServed": ["US", "CA"],
	"url": "{{ site.url }}/conversations/",
	"description": "Multi-channel chat sessions API — SMS, MMS, WhatsApp, and in-app chat — under one Twilio-compatible REST surface."
}
</script>

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Conversations</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Multi-channel chat sessions on one Twilio-compatible API.</h1>
			<p class="lede">VoiceTel Conversations gives application teams a single REST surface for SMS, MMS, WhatsApp, and in-app chat &mdash; same participant, same thread, same history &mdash; without re-implementing channel-specific glue for every project.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="{{ apiSpecs.voiceml.urlPath }}#tag/Conversations">Conversations API reference {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/signup/">Sign up</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set diagram = {
				title: "A participant on any channel, one conversation thread, your application over the API",
				nodes: [
					{ label: "Participant", value: "SMS · MMS · WhatsApp · chat", icon: "phone-vibrate" },
					{ label: "Conversation", value: "One thread, shared history", meta: "CH · IM · MB · IS", icon: "chat-square-text", accent: true },
					{ label: "Your app", value: "REST + signed webhooks", icon: "code-slash" }
				],
				links: [
					{ label: "channel", both: true },
					{ label: "API", both: true, accent: true }
				],
				meta: [
					{ k: "Host", v: "voiceml.voicetel.com" },
					{ k: "Webhooks", v: "HMAC-SHA256 signed" },
					{ k: "Sandboxes", v: "per-tenant Services" }
				]
			} %}
			{% include "partials/v2/diagram.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">What Conversations gives you</p>
			<h2 id="features-heading">One thread per participant, across every channel.</h2>
		</div>
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "chat-square-text", title: "Threaded multi-channel chat", body: "One conversation resource collects every message a participant sends &mdash; SMS, MMS, WhatsApp, or in-app &mdash; so application state stays consistent regardless of which channel a user replies on." },
			{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "Participants, roles, and users", body: "Add participants by phone number, WhatsApp ID, or chat user. Per-conversation roles assign permissions; reusable users carry identity across conversations." },
			{ icon: "broadcast-pin", title: "Signed webhook events", body: "Per-conversation or account-wide webhook subscriptions deliver message, participant, and read-receipt events to your endpoint. Same HMAC-SHA256 signature scheme as voice callbacks." },
			{ icon: "layers", title: "Service sandboxes", body: "Need to isolate workloads &mdash; staging from production, customer A from customer B? Conversations Services scope an entire chat environment under one parent service resource." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="compatibility" aria-labelledby="compatibility-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Compatibility</p>
				<h2 id="compatibility-heading">Twilio-compatible by design.</h2>
				<p class="lede">The Conversations endpoints mirror the Twilio v1 surface &mdash; same paths, same field names, same SID prefixes (<code>CH</code> for conversations, <code>IM</code> for messages, <code>MB</code> for participants, <code>IS</code> for services). Twilio's official client libraries work against <code>voiceml.voicetel.com</code> with a hostname + credential swap.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/voiceml/compatibility/#conversations">Endpoint map</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rows = [
					{ title: "Conversations", meta: "CRUD + create-with-participants", state: "Covered" },
					{ title: "Messages", meta: "CRUD · media · per-recipient receipts", state: "Covered" },
					{ title: "Participants", meta: "SMS · MMS · WhatsApp · chat bindings", state: "Covered" },
					{ title: "Webhooks", meta: "per-conversation and account-wide, signed", state: "Covered" },
					{ title: "Roles, Users, Credentials", meta: "identity · permissions · APNS / FCM keys", state: "Covered" },
					{ title: "Configuration", meta: "defaults · auto-routing per inbound address", state: "Covered" },
					{ title: "Services", meta: "scoped sandboxes with their own users and roles", state: "Covered" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/status-card.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
			<h2 id="faq-heading">Questions about Conversations.</h2>
		</div>
		{%- set faqs = [
			{ q: "Do my existing Twilio Conversations SDK clients work against VoiceTel?", a: "Yes &mdash; the v1 surface mirrors Twilio's. Point the client at <code>voiceml.voicetel.com</code> and use your VoiceTel account credentials. Paths, field names, and SID prefixes match." },
			{ q: "Which channels does VoiceTel Conversations support?", a: "SMS and MMS today via the same providers as <a href=\"/messaging/\">VoiceTel Messaging</a>. WhatsApp and in-app chat bindings follow the Twilio participant model; channel availability depends on which provider integrations are enabled on your account &mdash; contact support to confirm coverage for your use case." },
			{ q: "How do Conversations and Messaging differ?", a: "<a href=\"/messaging/\">Messaging</a> is the per-message API &mdash; send one SMS, get a delivery receipt. Conversations is the per-thread API &mdash; group every message a participant sends across channels into one resource, with shared history and participant state. Use Messaging for transactional fan-out; use Conversations when you need stateful multi-turn application chat." },
			{ q: "Are Conversations webhooks signed the same way as voice webhooks?", a: "Yes. HMAC-SHA256 over the canonicalised request body and URL, signed with your account auth token. See the <a href=\"/voiceml/migrate/#webhook-signatures\">webhook signatures guide</a>." },
			{ q: "Can I run staging and production traffic in the same account?", a: "Yes &mdash; create separate Conversations Services. Each service is a sandbox with its own users, roles, conversations, configuration, and webhooks under one parent account." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/faq.njk" %}

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Start your first conversation.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Open an account, swap your Twilio Conversations client to <code>voiceml.voicetel.com</code>, and send your first multi-channel thread the same hour. The official Twilio SDKs work as-is once the hostname and credentials are swapped.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Sign up {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ apiSpecs.voiceml.urlPath }}#tag/Conversations">API reference</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
